<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Vasa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vasa dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Vasa was a Swedish royal dynasty founded by Gustav I, who became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in 1523. Through Sigismund III, elected King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1587, a Polish branch ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> until the abdication of John II Casimir in 1668. Rivalry between the two branches over the Swedish crown led to a long series of Polish–Swedish wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-vasa.jpg" alt="House of Vasa" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armoiries_famille_Vasa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>With John II's death in 1532 the Upper Silesian Piasts died out, and Opole passed to the Bohemian crown under the Habsburgs, pledged at times to Brandenburg and the <b>Polish Vasas</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-opole">Duchy of Opole</a></li></ul></section>
